### Cloudflare Pages caching rules.
### Static assets are cache-busted manually (css/js via a ?v= query string,
### images via re-numbered filenames when replaced), so it's safe to cache
### them aggressively at the edge and in visitors' browsers. HTML documents
### are intentionally left on Cloudflare Pages' default no-cache behaviour
### so every deploy shows up immediately without a manual cache purge.

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400
